# Cursor Rules for {{projectName}}

## Project Architecture
This project uses the **{{pattern}}** architectural pattern.

{{#if (eq pattern "atomic")}}
### Atomic Design Structure
Components are organized in `{{basePath}}/components/` following atomic design:
- `atoms/` — Smallest reusable elements (buttons, inputs, labels)
- `molecules/` — Groups of atoms that form a simple UI component
- `organisms/` — Complex UI sections composed of molecules and atoms
- `templates/` — Page-level layouts
- `pages/` — Full route/page components

When creating components, always use:
```
npx rorg atom       # for atoms
npx rorg molecule   # for molecules
npx rorg organism   # for organisms
npx rorg template   # for templates
npx rorg page       # for pages
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "pages-components")}}
### Pages & Components Structure
- `{{basePath}}/components/` — Reusable UI components
- `{{basePath}}/pages/` — Route-level page components

When creating:
```
npx rorg component  # reusable components
npx rorg page       # page components
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "feature-first")}}
### Feature-First Structure
- `{{basePath}}/features/<feature>/` — Feature modules (components, hooks, utils, index.ts)
- `{{basePath}}/shared/` — Shared UI components used across features

When creating:
```
npx rorg feature    # new feature module
npx rorg shared     # shared component
```
{{/if}}

## File & Naming Conventions
- Component files: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g., `MyButton.tsx`)
- Each component lives in its own directory: `ComponentName/`
- Every component directory must have an `index.ts` re-export
{{#if separateCss}}- Styles: `ComponentName.module.css` (CSS Modules){{/if}}
{{#if includeTests}}- Tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx` using `@testing-library/react`{{/if}}

## TypeScript & React Rules
- Always use `React.FC<Props>` with a named props interface
- Use `React.ReactNode` for children props
- Export components as named exports, not default exports
- Props interface naming: `{ComponentName}Props`

## Code Style
- No `any` types — use proper TypeScript types
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)
{{#if separateCss}}- Use CSS Modules for all styles, never inline styles{{/if}}
- Use semantic HTML elements
